    "answer": {
      "short": "$f'(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}$ for $x>0$.",
      "worked": "Factor the numerator using the conjugate $\\sqrt{x}-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-1)(\\sqrt{x}+1)}{\\sqrt{x}+1}\\\\f(x)&=x^{1/2}-1,\\qquad x\\ge0\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2}\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
